      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I hear you loud and clear, and it is completely understandable why your body and mind reject these suggestions when your energy is already at zero. When the sheer cost of \"trying to fix this\" feels impossible, simply acknowledging that resting is not a failure but a necessary survival mechanism is perhaps the only step that should come first. You are not in a race; you are not failing, and asking for permission to stop moving isn't weakness, it is your mind telling you that you can't keep doing that. Please know that if all options feel like too much work right now, just lying still without judgment is a valid and worthy choice.",
      "source": "target",
